// Title: Cab File Extraction Via Wusa.EXE
// Sigma ID: 59b39960-5f9d-4a49-9cef-1e4d2c1d0cb9
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-04 | Modified: 2024-08-15
// ATT&CK: execution
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects execution of the "wusa.exe" (Windows Update Standalone Installer) utility to extract cab
//   using the "/extract" argument that is no longer supported.
// False positives:
//   - The "extract" flag still works on older 'wusa.exe' versions, which could be a legitimate use (monitor the path of the cab being extracted)
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20180331144337/https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2018/03/sanny-malware-delivery-method-updated-in-recently-observed-attacks.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wusa_cab_files_extraction.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\wusa.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/extract:"
